# Title: Suspicious Velociraptor Child Process
# ID: 4bc90587-e6ca-4b41-be0b-ed4d04e4ed0c
# Status: experimental
# Level: high
# Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2025-08-29
# Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.persistence, attack.t1219
# Description: Detects the suspicious use of the Velociraptor DFIR tool to execute other tools or download additional payloads, as seen in a campaign where it was abused for remote access and to stage further attacks.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((ParentImage="*\\Velociraptor.exe") AND (((CommandLine CONTAINS "msiexec" AND CommandLine CONTAINS "/i" AND CommandLine CONTAINS "http")) OR ((Image="*\\powershell.exe" OR Image="*\\powershell_ise.exe" OR Image="*\\pwsh.exe") AND (CommandLine CONTAINS "Invoke-WebRequest " OR CommandLine CONTAINS "IWR " OR CommandLine CONTAINS ".DownloadFile" OR CommandLine CONTAINS ".DownloadString")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAINS "code.exe" AND CommandLine CONTAINS "tunnel" AND CommandLine CONTAINS "--accept-server-license-terms"))))
